## Stack

Next.js (App Router) · TypeScript strict · MongoDB via Mongoose · Tailwind CSS ·
Zod · Vitest · pnpm

## Commands

- `pnpm dev` — dev server
- `pnpm build` — production build (must pass before any PR)
- `pnpm test` — run tests
- `pnpm lint` / `pnpm typecheck` — lint and types

## Architecture

- `src/app/` — routes, layouts, route handlers. Thin: validate → call service.
- `src/modules/<feature>/` — feature code: `components/`, `services/`, `schemas/`.
  Services own all business logic and DB access.
- `src/lib/db/` — connection singleton (`connect.ts`) + Mongoose models (`models/`).
- `src/lib/env.ts` — Zod-validated env. Never import from client components.

## Rules

- All external input is Zod-validated before reaching a service.
- Services return plain DTOs (`.lean()` + explicit mapping) — never Mongoose docs.
- Every server action and route handler checks auth itself.
- List queries are always paginated.
- Server components by default; `'use client'` on the smallest leaf that needs it.
- Every model file uses the `models.X ?? model('X', schema)` hot-reload guard.
- Conventional commits. No AI attribution or Co-Authored-By trailers, ever.

## Environment

Copy `.env.example` to `.env.local`. Required: `MONGODB_URI`, `AUTH_SECRET`.
